href is the serialized full URL. get(name) returns the first decoded value or null when absent; getAll(name) returns all decoded values in an array, or an empty array. topicURL builds the value using explicit topic and tag inputs.
```javascript
function topicURL(topic, tags) {
  const url = new URL("/study", "https://example.invalid");
  url.searchParams.set("topic", topic);
  for (const tag of tags) url.searchParams.append("tag", tag);
  return url.href;
}
const text = topicURL("read maps", ["a/b", "next"]);
console.log(text);
const parsed = new URL(text);
console.log(parsed.searchParams.get("topic"));
console.log(JSON.stringify(parsed.searchParams.getAll("tag")));
```
Output: https://example.invalid/study?topic=read+maps&tag=a%2Fb&tag=next, then read maps, then ["a/b","next"].

